FIFA 17 / CrossOver 26.3: CoreAudio fixes.  BUGS.md #4.

The startup deadlock was NOT wine's: /Library/Audio/Plug-Ins/HAL/MSTeamsAudioDevice.driver
stops answering, and any process that points an AudioUnit at its device hangs forever inside
the CoreAudio HAL -- reproducible with a 40-line native program, no wine involved.  Chasing it
did turn up two real wine bugs on the way, both fixed here:

  dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c       capture authorization is checked three calls too
                                           late, after the input AudioUnit has already been
                                           created and pointed at the device; on a host that
                                           cannot show the permission dialog that call never
                                           returns.  Ask first, in get_audiounit(), so every
                                           entry point is covered, and cache the answer.
                                           Also adds WINE_COREAUDIO_EXCLUDE, to skip a wedged
                                           device by name without uninstalling its driver.

  dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/authorization.m   the permission request waited DISPATCH_TIME_FOREVER.
                                           Bounded to 5s, treating a timeout as "not granted".
                                           The completion handler can now outlive the wait, so
                                           the shared state is refcounted instead of living on
                                           the caller's stack.

